#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Accessibility statement"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "A starting point for an accessibility statement: commitment, standard, measures, known limitations, feedback and the date of the last review. Edit every section to match your own site before publishing."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:17
msgid "Our commitment"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:21
msgid "We want everyone to be able to learn with us, whatever device they use and however they read, hear, move or think. This statement covers this website and the courses on it."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:25
msgid "The standard we aim for"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:29
msgid "We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA. We check new pages and courses against it before they go live."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:33
msgid "What we do"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:39
msgid "Every page can be used with a keyboard alone, with a visible focus outline and a link to skip to the main content."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:43
msgid "Text and buttons meet the AA contrast ratio in every colour scheme we offer, including the dark scheme."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:47
msgid "Images that carry meaning have text alternatives, and form fields have visible labels."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:51
msgid "Text resizes to 200% without loss of content, and nothing on the site moves or animates on its own."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:55
msgid "Course videos have captions and transcripts."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:61
msgid "Known limitations"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:65
msgid "Some older course downloads (PDF worksheets) are not yet fully tagged for screen readers. We are replacing them course by course; ask us for an accessible copy of any file in the meantime."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:69
msgid "Tell us about a problem"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:73
msgid "If something on this site does not work for you, tell us what page you were on and what happened. We reply within five working days and will provide the content another way while we fix it."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:73
msgid "Contact us about accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:77
msgid "About this statement"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/accessibility-statement.php:81
msgid "This statement was last reviewed on [date]. Replace this sentence with the date of your own review."
msgstr ""

